Potentially useful columns and why  
• DICOM_ALL."PatientID": patient identifier needed in the output.  
• DICOM_ALL."StudyInstanceUID": study identifier needed in the output.  
• DICOM_ALL."StudyDate": will be filtered to year 2001 and included in the output.  
• QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS."segmentationInstanceUID": has to equal DICOM_ALL."SOPInstanceUID" to join SR measurements with the corresponding segmentation object.  
• QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS."Quantity": VARIANT holding the JSON object that contains the measurement CodeMeaning (e.g. “Elongation”, “Volume from Voxel Summation”).  
• QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS."Value": numeric measurement itself (will be aggregated with MAX).  
• QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS."findingSite": VARIANT containing JSON with the site CodeMeaning (e.g. “Lung”) – required in the output.  
• QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS."PatientID": useful cross‑check of the join.  
• DICOM_ALL."SOPInstanceUID": connects a segmentation object stored in DICOM_ALL to the SR row in QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS.  

Basic conditions that will be used later  
• DICOM_ALL."StudyDate" BETWEEN '20010101' AND '20011231' (simple date‐range filter).  
• QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING IN (…) to pick only the eleven measurements of interest.  
• QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS."segmentationInstanceUID" = DICOM_ALL."SOPInstanceUID" to join the two tables.  
• GROUP BY DICOM_ALL."PatientID", DICOM_ALL."StudyInstanceUID", DICOM_ALL."StudyDate", QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS."findingSite":"CodeMeaning"::STRING.  

Below are ten incremental Snowflake queries (all limited to 20 rows) that walk from simple exploration to the fully‑formed answer.  
Every identifier is wrapped in double quotes, and queries are annotated.

```sql
-- 1) Distinct study dates so we can verify 2001 values really exist
SELECT DISTINCT "StudyDate"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
ORDER BY "StudyDate"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Sample of patients whose study year is 2001
SELECT "PatientID", "StudyInstanceUID", "StudyDate"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "StudyDate" BETWEEN '20010101' AND '20011231'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Peek at JSON structure of the findingSite field
SELECT "findingSite", 
       "findingSite":"CodeMeaning"::STRING  AS "FindingSite_CodeMeaning"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Inspect JSON inside Quantity to see available measurement names
SELECT DISTINCT "Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING AS "Measurement_CodeMeaning"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Verify that all eleven desired measurements are present
SELECT DISTINCT "Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS
WHERE "Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING IN (
  'Elongation', 'Flatness', 'Least Axis in 3D Length', 'Major Axis in 3D Length',
  'Maximum 3D Diameter of a Mesh', 'Minor Axis in 3D Length', 'Sphericity',
  'Surface Area of Mesh', 'Surface to Volume Ratio',
  'Volume from Voxel Summation', 'Volume of Mesh'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Quick inner join on SOPInstanceUID↔segmentationInstanceUID
SELECT d."PatientID",
       d."StudyInstanceUID",
       d."StudyDate",
       q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING      AS "Measurement_Type",
       q."Value"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL                 d
JOIN   IDC.IDC_V17.QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS q
     ON q."segmentationInstanceUID" = d."SOPInstanceUID"
WHERE  d."StudyDate" BETWEEN '20010101' AND '20011231'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Same join but include finding site CodeMeaning
SELECT d."PatientID",
       d."StudyInstanceUID",
       d."StudyDate",
       q."findingSite":"CodeMeaning"::STRING   AS "FindingSite",
       q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING      AS "Measurement_Type",
       q."Value"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL                 d
JOIN   IDC.IDC_V17.QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS q
     ON q."segmentationInstanceUID" = d."SOPInstanceUID"
WHERE  d."StudyDate" BETWEEN '20010101' AND '20011231'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Aggregate: max value per study + measurement (single measurement example)
SELECT d."PatientID",
       d."StudyInstanceUID",
       d."StudyDate",
       q."findingSite":"CodeMeaning"::STRING        AS "FindingSite",
       MAX(q."Value")                               AS "Max_VolumeVoxel"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL                 d
JOIN   IDC.IDC_V17.QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS q
     ON q."segmentationInstanceUID" = d."SOPInstanceUID"
WHERE  d."StudyDate" BETWEEN '20010101' AND '20011231'
  AND  q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Volume from Voxel Summation'
GROUP  BY d."PatientID", d."StudyInstanceUID", d."StudyDate",
          q."findingSite":"CodeMeaning"::STRING
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Conditional aggregation for the eleven measurements (still limited)
SELECT d."PatientID",
       d."StudyInstanceUID",
       d."StudyDate",
       q."findingSite":"CodeMeaning"::STRING                                   AS "FindingSite",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Elongation'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_Elongation",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Flatness'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_Flatness",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Least Axis in 3D Length'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_LeastAxis3D",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Major Axis in 3D Length'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_MajorAxis3D",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Maximum 3D Diameter of a Mesh'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_Max3DDiameter",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Minor Axis in 3D Length'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_MinorAxis3D",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Sphericity'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_Sphericity",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Surface Area of Mesh'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_SurfaceArea",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Surface to Volume Ratio'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_SurfVolRatio",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Volume from Voxel Summation'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_VolumeVoxel",
       MAX(CASE WHEN q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING = 'Volume of Mesh'
                THEN q."Value" END)                                            AS "Max_VolumeMesh"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL                 d
JOIN   IDC.IDC_V17.QUANTITATIVE_MEASUREMENTS q
     ON q."segmentationInstanceUID" = d."SOPInstanceUID"
WHERE  d."StudyDate" BETWEEN '20010101' AND '20011231'
  AND  q."Quantity":"CodeMeaning"::STRING IN (
       'Elongation','Flatness','Least Axis in 3D Length',
       'Major Axis in 3D Length','Maximum 3D Diameter of a Mesh',
       'Minor Axis in 3D Length','Sphericity','Surface Area of Mesh',
       'Surface to Volume Ratio','Volume from Voxel Summation','Volume of Mesh')
GROUP  BY d."PatientID", d."StudyInstanceUID", d."StudyDate",
          q."findingSite":"CodeMeaning"::STRING
LIMIT 20;
```

